1. Kf7 $1 {Two stalemates save Black after the thematic try 1.Kg6.}  (1. Kg6 $2
e5 2. Bxe5 Kg8 3. Nd4 (3. Bxg7 {stalemate} ) 3... Ne6 $1 4. Nxe6 {stalemate}  (
4. Nc6 Nf8+ $10) ) 1... e5 2. Bxe5 Kh7 3. Bd6 $1 (3. Ne3 $2 Nf5 $1 {like in the
thematic try} )  (3. Bf4 $2 Nf5 $10) 3... Nf5 4. Bf8 Nh4 {The strongest
defence.}  (4... Nh6+ 5. Kf6 Ng4+ 6. Kf5 {leads to the position in the mainline
(move 10) } ) 5. Nd4 (5. Ne3 $2 Nf3 $1 $10) 5... Ng6 6. Bg7 Nh8+ (6... Nf4 7.
Nf3 Ne6 8. Bb2 Ng7 (8... Nd8+ 9. Ke7 $18) 9. Bc1 Nf5 10. Kf6 Ng7 11. Ng5+ Kg8
12. Ba3) 7. Kf6 (7. Kf8 $2 Nf7 $1 $10) 7... Nf7 (7... Kg8 8. Bh6 Nf7 9. Bf4 $18
)  (7... Ng6 8. Ne6 Kg8 9. Bh6 Kh7 10. Bd2 $18) 8. Bf8 (8. Nf3 $2 Kg8 $1 $10)
8... Nh6 9. Nc2 $3 {One of these "invisible moves": the white knight not only
moves away from the action, it also came from c2 on move 5 (switchback)!}  (9.
Kg5 {loses time} 9... Nf7+ 10. Kf6 Nh6) 9... Ng4+ 10. Kf5 (10. Kg5 $2 Ne5 $10)
10... Nh6+ (10... Nh2 11. Kf4 $18) 11. Kg5 Nf7+ 12. Kf6 Nh6 (12... Kg8 13. Bb4
Nh6 14. Ne3 Nf7 15. Nf5 $18) 13. Ne3 {and White wins easily, e.g., } 13... Ng8+
14. Kg5 Kh8 15. Kg6 1-0

