[Site "?"]
[Date "2026.??.??"]
[Round "?"]
[White "Franzoni=G Neuenschwander=B"]
[Black "(=0016.02e7f4)"]
[Result "1/2-1/2"]
[FEN "n7/4K1B1/8/2p5/1p3k2/8/4n3/8 w - - 0 1"]
1. Kd6 {That the c1 is under control due ot Bh6+ gives White hope.... } 1... c4
2. Kc5 c3 3. Kxb4 c2 4. Kb3 c1=N+ {Three knights win against one bishop. White
must exchange the bishop against one of the knights.} 5. Kc2 Ke4 6. Kd2 $1 (6.
Kd1 $2 Kd3 $19)  (6. Bb2 $2 Nd3 $19) 6... Kf3 7. Kc2 $1 {Otherwise the knight
escapes via b3.} 7... Na2 8. Kb3 Nac1+ (8... Nec1+ 9. Kb2 $1 {and Bh6} ) 9. Kc2
Ke4 10. Kd2 Nb6 11. Bh6 $3 {The most difficult move of the study: the threat is
Ke1 (Kd1)}  (11. Bb2 $2 Nc4+ 12. Kc2 Nd3 $19) 11... Kf3 (11... Nc4+ 12. Ke1 $1
$10 (12. Kd1 $2 Nb2+ 13. Kc2 (13. Ke1 Nbd3+ $19) 13... Ncd3 $19) ) 12. Kc2 Na2
13. Bd2 $1 {and the white king attacks the knight on a2 in the next move, after
which White escapes by a bishop-knight exchange .}  (13. Kb3 $2 Nac3 $1 $19)
1/2-1/2

